[2026-07-25T15:13:00.000Z] RESOLUTION: PDF EXPORT & LIVE GEMINI AI FEEDBACK FIX
CATEGORY: Web Desktop PDF Share API Failure & Schema Constraint 400
ROOT CAUSE 1: Printing.sharePdf calls navigator.share on Web, which is a mobile-only Web Share API. On Desktop web browsers (Chrome/Edge/Firefox on Windows/macOS), navigator.share throws TypeError or fails silently.
FIX 1: Created pdf_downloader.dart (web conditional export header) using native HTML Blob Object URL anchor download (html.AnchorElement + html.Blob), triggering immediate direct PDF file download in all desktop and mobile browsers.

ROOT CAUSE 2: Passing complex 600-line Zod schema to Google AI Studio API via output: { schema: evaluationSchema } caused Google AI Studio to reject the OpenAPI responseSchema with HTTP 400: "The specified schema produces a constraint that has too many states for serving."
FIX 2: Configured responseMimeType: 'application/json' in Genkit generation config and added robust JSON parsing & ensureScoreObj safety wrapper to prevent NaN/TypeError crashes.

STATUS: PERMANENTLY RESOLVED & VERIFIED CLEAN
